Vita: the log file is written at the info level, and error and fatal lines reach the platform.

Dusklight opens a log file at every launch (ux0:data/TwilitRealm/Dusklight/logs) and writes it
at the debug level: a line or two for every process the game creates and for every create
request, about 3,600 lines in two minutes of stage loads (Vita3K, a tour of the Forest Temple's
rooms). On the console that is formatting and file writes on the memory card during every load,
for lines only a developer reads. At the info level the file keeps the build, the platform, the
configuration and every warning, error and fatal message, which is what a bug report needs. A
level asked for on the command line still applies (standard.apply_to runs after this line).

When the game stops itself (Log.fatal, then abort) the reason is one line of text, and what led
to it is a few error lines before it (a heap that could not allocate names itself, the size
asked for and its free blocks). In Vita3K the log file ended before those lines in three runs
out of three (the process dies with the file's last block unwritten), so the reason was lost.
Error lines and the fatal line are now also handed to the platform (borealis' divert and onFatal
hooks), which writes them as receipts. Nothing changes outside TARGET_VITA.

--- a/src/dusk/logging.cpp
+++ b/src/dusk/logging.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,11 @@
 
 using namespace std::literals::string_view_literals;
 
+#if TARGET_VITA
+extern "C" void twv_vita_fatal_text(const char* text, unsigned size) __attribute__((weak));
+extern "C" void twv_vita_error_text(const char* text, unsigned size) __attribute__((weak));
+#endif
+
 namespace {
 constexpr std::string_view kStubFragments[] = {
     "is a stub"sv,
@@ -29,6 +34,13 @@
 
 bool divert_stub_messages(const borealis::log::Message& message) {
     ZoneScoped;
+#if TARGET_VITA
+    // Vita (patches/dusklight/0074): an error line is also handed to the platform, which keeps the
+    // first ones of a run as receipts (what the game says before it stops is a run of error lines).
+    if (message.level >= borealis::LogLevel::Error && twv_vita_error_text) {
+        twv_vita_error_text(message.text.data(), static_cast<unsigned>(message.text.size()));
+    }
+#endif
     if (!StubLogEnabled || !is_for_stub_log(message.text)) {
         return false;
     }
@@ -40,7 +52,19 @@
 void dusk::InitializeLogging(
     const std::filesystem::path& cacheDir, const borealis::cli::StandardOptions& standard) {
     borealis::log::Options options{};
+#if TARGET_VITA
+    // Vita (patches/dusklight/0074): the log file is on the memory card and the debug level writes
+    // a line or two for every process the game creates (about 3,600 lines in two minutes of stage
+    // loads). Info keeps the build, the configuration, every warning, error and fatal message.
+    options.level = borealis::LogLevel::Info;
+    // The text of a fatal message also goes to the platform (twilight-vita:
+    // platform/vita/runtime/fault_receipts.cpp), which records it beside the abort it leads to.
+    options.onFatal = [](std::string_view text) {
+        if (twv_vita_fatal_text) twv_vita_fatal_text(text.data(), static_cast<unsigned>(text.size()));
+    };
+#else
     options.level = borealis::LogLevel::Debug;
+#endif
     options.fileDirectory = cacheDir.empty() ? std::filesystem::path{} : cacheDir / "logs";
     options.filePrefix = "dusklight";
     options.legacyFilePrefixes = {"dusk"};
